.* QUIFCNUSG: WRKFCNUSG (the functions; option 2 prompts CHGFCNUSG,
.* option 5 is DSPFCNUSG) and DSPFCNUSG, one function and the profiles
.* with usage of their own, two to a row as the oracle lays them out.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE=ACTION.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=IDCL BASETYPE='CHAR 30'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 42'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=VALCL BASETYPE='CHAR 50'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=USERCL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=TYPECL BASETYPE='CHAR 13'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=USAGECL BASETYPE='CHAR 12'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPT CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNID CLASS=IDCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNNAME CLASS=NAMECL.
:VAR NAME=FCNDESC CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNDESC2 CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNPROD CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNGRP CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNDFT CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=FCNALLOBJ CLASS=VALCL.
:VAR NAME=USER1 CLASS=USERCL.
:VAR NAME=TYPE1 CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=USAGE1 CLASS=USAGECL.
:VAR NAME=USER2 CLASS=USERCL.
:VAR NAME=TYPE2 CLASS=TYPECL.
:VAR NAME=USAGE2 CLASS=USAGECL.
:LISTDEF NAME=FUNCTIONS VARS='OPT FCNID FCNNAME'.
:LISTDEF NAME=USERS VARS='USER1 TYPE1 USAGE1 USER2 TYPE2 USAGE2'.
:KEYL NAME=WRKKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F5 ACTION='RETURN 5'.F5=Refresh
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:KEYL NAME=DSPKEYS HELP=KEYSHLP.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F17 ACTION=TOP.F17=Top
:KEYI KEY=F18 ACTION=BOTTOM.F18=Bottom
:KEYI KEY=PAGEUP ACTION=PAGEUP.
:KEYI KEY=PAGEDOWN ACTION=PAGEDOWN.
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=WRKFCNUSG KEYL=WRKKEYS HELP=WRKFCNH ENTER='RETURN 0'.Work with Function Usage
:TOPINST.Type options, press Enter.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=FUNCTIONS ACTLEN=1 SCROLL=YES.(No functions found.)
:LISTACT OPTION=2 ENTER='CMD ?CHGFCNUSG FCNID(&FCNID.)' HELP='WRKFCNUSG/OPTIONS'.2=Change usage
:LISTACT OPTION=5 ENTER='RETURN 55' HELP='WRKFCNUSG/OPTIONS'.5=Display usage
:LISTCOL VAR=OPT USAGE=INPUT HELP='WRKFCNUSG/OPT'.Opt
:LISTCOL VAR=FCNID USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNID'.Function ID
:LISTCOL VAR=FCNNAME USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNNAME'.Function Name
:ELIST.
:CMDLINE SIZE=SHORT.Parameters for option 2 or command
:EPANEL.
:PANEL NAME=DSPFCNUSG KEYL=DSPKEYS HELP=DSPFCNH BOTSEP=NONE ENTER='RETURN 0'.Display Function Usage
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=26.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=FCNID USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNID'.Function ID
:DATAI VAR=FCNNAME USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNNAME'.Function name
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=26.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAC.
:DATAI VAR=FCNDESC USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNDESC'.Description
:DATAI VAR=FCNDESC2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNDESC'.
:DATAC.
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH=2.
:DATACOL WIDTH=26.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAI VAR=FCNPROD USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNPROD'.Product
:DATAI VAR=FCNGRP USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNGRP'.Group
:EDATA.
:DATA DEPTH=4.
:DATACOL WIDTH=44.
:DATACOL WIDTH=78.
:DATAC.
:DATAI VAR=FCNDFT USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNDFT'.Default authority
:DATAI VAR=FCNALLOBJ USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/FCNALLOBJ'.*ALLOBJ special authority
:DATAC.
:EDATA.
:LIST DEPTH='*' LISTDEF=USERS SCROLL=YES.(No user profiles have usage information)
:LISTCOL VAR=USER1 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USER'.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE1 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=USAGE1 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USAGE'.Usage
:LISTCOL VAR=USER2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USER'.User
:LISTCOL VAR=TYPE2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:LISTCOL VAR=USAGE2 USAGE=OUTPUT HELP='FLD/USAGE'.Usage
:ELIST.
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=WRKFCNH.Work with Function Usage - Help
:P.This display lists the functions a profile can be allowed or denied
apart from the authority to objects. Option 2 changes a function's
default, whether *ALLOBJ special authority allows it, or a profile's
usage; option 5 shows them.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=DSPFCNH.Display Function Usage - Help
:P.This display shows one function: what it controls, whether profiles
may use it by default and whether *ALLOBJ special authority allows it,
then the user and group profiles with usage of their own. A profile's
own usage comes first, then its groups', then *ALLOBJ, then the
default.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME=KEYSHLP.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display.
:PT.F4=Prompt
:PD.Prompts the command on the command line.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the functions again.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display.
:PT.F17=Top
:PD.Shows the first entries of the list.
:PT.F18=Bottom
:PD.Shows the last entries of the list.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKFCNUSG/OPTIONS'.Options
:PARML.
:PT.2=Change usage
:PD.Prompts CHGFCNUSG for the function.
:PT.5=Display usage
:PD.Shows the function and the profiles with usage of their own.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKFCNUSG/OPT'.Opt
:P.Type the option to use on the function.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNID'.Function ID
:P.The function's identifier, as programs and CHGFCNUSG name it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNNAME'.Function name
:P.The function's name.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNDESC'.Description
:P.What the function controls.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNPROD'.Product
:P.The product the function belongs to.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNGRP'.Group
:P.The group of functions it belongs to, *NONE for none.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNDFT'.Default authority
:P.Whether a profile with no usage of its own, and no group with one,
may use the function.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/FCNALLOBJ'.*ALLOBJ special authority
:P.*USED: a profile with *ALLOBJ special authority may use the function
whatever the default. *NOTUSED: it counts for nothing here.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USER'.User
:P.A user or group profile with usage of its own.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/TYPE'.Type
:P.Whether the profile is a user or a group profile.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/USAGE'.Usage
:P.*ALLOWED or *DENIED, for the profile.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
